proposals.what:
The landing's primary pill becomes 'Start my plan'; 'Set it up step by step' opens the wizard. One tap sends POST /api/plan with plan.defaults(learner):
- current: mean3, else the latest midpoint, else 500 marked estimated;
- target: min(round10(current+100), 780);
- exam: learners.exam_date, else the first SAT_DATES entry at least 28 days away, marked booked=false;
- minutes: the median minutes of the last 21 active days, rounded to a chip (else 45);
- days: the weekdays actually studied most (else Mon–Fri);
- tests: weekly module;
- focus: the suggestions from the points model;
- extras: the defaults.
The response opens the Plan tab with a 'Built from your results' banner. It lists the six assumptions as editable chips ('Target 660 ✎ · Nov 7 · not booked ✎ · 45 min × 5 ✎ · Weekly module ✎ · Focus Advanced Math ✎ · Rechecks on ✎'). Each chip edits in place through a popover and PATCH, with no wizard. The banner stays for 3 days or until dismissed. For a new student, day 1's first task is the 12-question placement (see parity gap 'Step 1'). When it finishes, the plan re-bases current and shows a toast with Undo: 'Starting score set to 540 from your placement'.

On the first visit after a week's last study day, a sheet 'Week 3 review · Sep 21–27' opens once. It can be reopened from 'Review week' in the WeekStrip header. Receipts come first, as a grid: 'Days 4/5 · 3h 10m of 3h 45m · 212 questions · 71% right · traps closed 6, opened 2 · Circles Learning → Getting there · Checkpoint +40 · forecast 650 → 670'. Next comes 'Next week', prefilled by plan.propose_goals():
- at most 3 goals, each of type close_traps {family or labels, n}, tier {topic, tier, pct, min_n 10}, checkpoint {date} or minutes {n};
- 7 per-day minute selects;
- days off;
- a 'Swap a focus skill' select.
Controls: × per goal, 'Add goal', and 'Save week', which writes plan_overrides for that week. The week header then shows 'Goals 2/3' as chips with glyphs (met ✓, open ○, missed –), evaluated live. A missed goal offers 'Carry to next week'. Server: plan_weeks(plan, n, goals JSON, reviewed TEXT NULL); GET and PUT /api/plan/{id}/week/{n}. plan.week_review() reuses the stats the Progress tab already computes.

Trap sheet: GET /api/plan/{id}/trapsheet returns up to 10 entries from the misconception profile (falling back to trap labels). Each entry has:
- the family name and its hits;
- one freshly generated item (a new seed, so no seen key; R19);
- the trap option marked 'Your trap', plus the key, the rationale and a one-line 'Tell' (the reason text).
It renders at /plan/?print=traps as a phone-readable page and a 2-page print (@media print, A4/Letter). Final phase schedules 'Trap gauntlet · 10 questions, one per trap on your sheet' 3 days out, and 'Read your trap sheet · 5 min' (tick to done) as the eve's only task, beside the checklist. Week pack: PlanMenu 'Print…' gains 'This week's worksheets'. For every remaining study day of the viewed week, it prints the day's focus set through Practice's worksheet renderer, headed 'Thu Sep 24 · Focus · Circles, Percentages · 18 questions · 28 min'. Answer keys and rationales go at the back ('Include answer keys', on by default). Each sheet carries a code such as 'W-7K2P'. Entering answers at /practice/session/?ws=W-7K2P files them and counts toward that day.
